{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cc714ea573ced272cbeb576a988e9871a9849c3b98bf7c627101d0958b54c72f","digest":{"component_or_area":"review bot retrigger","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py","TRIGGER_TOKEN","_TOKEN_RE","_RETIRED_TOKEN_RE","infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template","_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE","_refusal_message","post_comment","recheck","rerun-llm-review","recheck-review"],"problem_keywords":["ci trigger collision","gerrit chatops matcher","substring matching","trigger word rename","bot reply injection"],"propositions":["The old trigger word 'recheck-review' collides with external CI ChatOps mapper 'recheck' because the substring-based matcher in gerrit_to_platform.ini triggers Verified workflow on any comment containing 'recheck'.","Bot reply texts contain the retired trigger word, causing the bot's own Gerrit comments to re-dispatch the spurious CI Verified workflow.","A hard cutover to the new trigger 'rerun-llm-review' eliminates the substring collision while a refusal reply informs users of the new word.","All bot-posted replies must be scrubbed of any mapped CI ChatOps trigger keywords to prevent self-inflicted CI dispatch.","The new trigger word must pass substring-disjointness tests against the ini template parsed at test time to prevent future collisions."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787327801875492001,"uuid":"85ad2fc3-82a8-4d15-8a4a-9bff71f1b17d"}